.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt ZSTDIR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zstdir ,
.Nm unzstdir
.Nd compress and extract directories with zstd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cfqv
.Op Fl L Ar level
.Op Fl T Ar threads
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Ar dir ...
.Nm
.Op Fl fqv
.Op Fl T Ar threads
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Ar archive ...
.Nm
.Fl d
.Op Fl fqv
.Op Fl T Ar threads
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Op Ar archive | Fl
.Nm unzstdir
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar archive ...
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
packs a directory into a zstd-compressed tar archive, or unpacks one, in a
single step.
The mode is chosen from each argument: a directory is compressed into
.Ar dir Ns Pa .tar.zst ,
and a zstd file (recognized by its contents, not its name) is extracted.
.Nm unzstdir
is the same program and always extracts, like
.Fl d .
.Pp
Outputs are written next to their inputs.
Archives are first written to a temporary file and extractions to a
temporary directory, renamed into place only when complete, so a failed or
interrupted run leaves nothing behind.
An existing archive is only overwritten with
.Fl f ;
an existing directory is never replaced.
.Pp
Archives are plain tar inside zstd and can be read and written by other
tools, for example
.Ql tar --zstd -xf dir.tar.zst
or
.Ql zstd -dc dir.tar.zst | tar -xf - .
Entries are stored under the directory's name, so plain tar also recreates
the directory itself.
.Ss Extraction
When an archive holds a single top-level directory, its contents become the
output directory: the archive name without its
.Pa .tar.zst ,
.Pa .tar.zstd ,
.Pa .tzst ,
.Pa .zst
or
.Pa .zstd
suffix, or
.Ar path
given with
.Fl o .
An archive with several top-level entries is extracted into that directory
instead of spilling them into the current one.
When reading standard input without
.Fl o ,
the archive's single top-level directory is created in the current
directory.
.Pp
Entries that would land outside the output directory, through
.Ql .. ,
absolute paths or symbolic links, are rejected.
Regular files, directories, symbolic links and hard links are extracted
with their permission bits (minus the umask; setuid, setgid and sticky bits
are dropped) and modification times.
Ownership is not restored.
The
.Pa ._*
AppleDouble files that macOS tar adds to carry extended attributes are
skipped.
.Ss Compression
Regular files, directories and symbolic links are archived; symbolic links
are stored as links, not followed.
Devices, sockets and FIFOs are skipped with a warning, and hard links are
stored as separate files.
Extended attributes and ACLs are not stored.
.Pp
With more than one thread, the archive is written as a series of
independently compressed zstd frames, which any zstd decoder reads as one
stream.
This lets compression use several cores at the cost of a slightly lower
ratio.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl -decompress
Extract.
Without an
.Ar archive ,
or with
.Fl ,
the archive is read from standard input.
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ns = Ns Ar path
Name of the archive when compressing, or of the directory to create when
extracting.
Only valid with a single input.
.It Fl c , Fl -stdout
Write the archive to standard output instead of a file.
Only valid when compressing a single directory.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Overwrite an existing archive, write an archive to a terminal, or read one
from a terminal.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
List each entry on standard error as it is processed.
Given twice, also print a summary for each input: the input and output,
the number of files, directories and symbolic links, the size before and
after, the ratio and space saved, and the time and throughput.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Do not print warnings.
.It Fl L , Fl -level Ns = Ns Ar level
Compression level from 1 to 22; the default is 3.
Levels are mapped to the four speed tiers of the Go zstd encoder used:
1\(en2 fastest, 3\(en5 default, 6\(en9 better, 10 and above best.
.It Fl T , Fl -threads Ns = Ns Ar threads
Number of threads to use; 0, the default, means one per CPU, up to 8.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
An error occurred.
With several inputs, the others are still processed.
.It 2
Invalid command line.
.It 130
Interrupted.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compress
.Pa photos/
into
.Pa photos.tar.zst ,
then extract it again:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstdir photos
zstdir photos.tar.zst
.Ed
.Pp
Choose the output names:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstdir -o backup.tar.zst photos
zstdir -o restored backup.tar.zst
.Ed
.Pp
Copy a directory to another host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstdir -c project | ssh host zstdir -d
.Ed
.Pp
Compress several directories, with a summary for each:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstdir -vv src docs assets
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr zstd 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An arjkb ,
.Lk https://github.com/arjkb/zstdir
